{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"variable class variable class","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md","fileName":"Variable Class.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Variable Class","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Analytic Data Preparation]] · [[Data Quality and Missing Data]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"variable class variable class","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Variable Class.md","fileName":"Variable Class.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Variable Class","heading":"Variable Class","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A variable class describes how statistical software interprets a column, such as numeric, integer, character, factor, or date. The same visible values can behave differently in summaries and models depending on their class.\n\nClass must reflect analytic meaning. A coded category stored as a number may otherwise be treated as continuous, while a date stored as text cannot participate correctly in date arithmetic. Checking and deliberately converting classes prevents these implicit modeling errors.\n\nThe book emphasizes deliberate conversion of imported character fields to factors, text dates to date objects, and mislabeled numerics to quantitative values. A class is therefore an analytic decision as well as a storage property.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","